# Model files — public API documentation

When creating or editing hand-written model code (JSON DTOs, enums, value objects) under any `**/models/**` path:

- **MUST** add a `///` doc comment on every **public** class, enum, mixin, extension, typedef, and top-level declaration.
- **MUST** add a `///` on every **public** field, getter, setter, and constructor (and on each enum value if it is not self-explanatory).
- Use `[fieldName]` in doc comments to reference other members when it helps. Prefer one short line per item; add a second paragraph for JSON/API edge cases, nullability, or units.
- `**/*.g.dart` is already excluded at the package root; do not add docs inside generated part files.

These expectations are for agents and review; the analyzer is not configured to require `public_member_api_docs` on models.
